{"title":"25","section":"500i","heading":"Omitted","lead":"","tree":[],"notes":[{"topic":"editorialNotes","text":"Editorial Notes"},{"topic":"codification","text":"Codification Section, act Sept. 1, 1937, ch. 897, § 10, 50 Stat. 901, which provided for alienation of reindeer or interests, was omitted from the Code as being of special and not general application."}],"sourceCredit":"","releasePoint":"119-102","ancestors":[{"type":"title","num":"Title 25—","heading":"INDIANS","identifier":"/us/usc/t25"},{"type":"chapter","num":"CHAPTER 14—","heading":"MISCELLANEOUS","identifier":"/us/usc/t25/ch14"},{"type":"subchapter","num":"SUBCHAPTER VII—","heading":"REINDEER INDUSTRY","identifier":"/us/usc/t25/ch14/schVII"}]}